From: enij90 <226572015+enij90@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] usb: typec: ucsi: glink: C2 keeps the data lanes while connected

The c2-select switch from 0012 only moved when exactly one connector was
connected and did nothing when both were. A charger or hub on C1 that came
up first left the lanes on C1 and the controller on C2 had no USB until C1
was unplugged; the same happened at boot. Prefer C2 whenever it is
connected and use C1 otherwise.

Taken from https://github.com/enij90/armada-tb321fu (Lenovo Legion Tab Gen 3 / Y700 2025,
TB321FU, SM8650).
---
--- a/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi_glink.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi_glink.c
@@ -300,11 +300,16 @@
 		c1_connected = ucsi->connector_connected[0];
 		c2_connected = ucsi->connector_connected[1];
 
-		if (c1_connected && !c2_connected) {
-			gpiod_set_value_cansleep(ucsi->c2_select, 0);
-		} else if (!c1_connected && c2_connected) {
+		/*
+		 * The data lanes follow C2 whenever it is connected: on the
+		 * TB321FU it is the short-side port of the attached controller,
+		 * which must keep USB when a charger or hub is plugged into C1,
+		 * in whatever order the two connect (also at boot).
+		 */
+		if (c2_connected)
 			gpiod_set_value_cansleep(ucsi->c2_select, 1);
-		}
+		else if (c1_connected)
+			gpiod_set_value_cansleep(ucsi->c2_select, 0);
 	}
 
 	dev_dbg(ucsi->dev,
